# --- s065 Book I d.26 q.2 (pp. 102–104)
n("n1175","s065-01","vtrum relatio in creatura differat realiter a fundamento","la","source","The doctrine follows Scotus, *Ord.* II d. 1 qq. 4–5 (Wadding) against Henry of Ghent: relation is really distinct from its foundation. Scotus has no *Ord.* I d. 26 q. 2.","verified")
n("n1176","s065-01","omne quod est ad aliud est aliquid ab eo","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* VII 1.2 (*omnis essentia quae relative dicitur est etiam aliquid excepto relativo*). B: *ad aliquid est aliud ab eo*. A’s *aliquid* matches Augustine. B checked.","verified")
n("n1177","s065-04","Aureolum","la","historical","Peter Auriol OFM († 1322). His view that relation is a being of reason is in his *Scriptum* I d. 30 (locus not checked).","probable")
n("n1178","s065-05","opinio Henrici","la","source","Henry of Ghent (cf. *Quodl.* V q. 2; IX q. 3): a relation is not a thing distinct from its foundation, since a new relation comes to a thing without change in it. Scotus reports and refutes this in *Ord.* II d. 1 q. 4 (Wadding, checked locally).","verified")
n("n1179","s065-05","fundamentum sine relatione","la","textual","B: *fundamentum esset sine relatione*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1180","s065-06","Hec etiam patet. quia distinguntur essentialiter","la","textual","B: *distinguuntur realiter*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1181","s065-07","formaliter dicitur filius","la","textual","B: *formaliter dicitur saluis*, corrupt. B checked.","certain")
n("n1182","s065-07","Sed suppleret vicem terminationis per primam sequeretur quod haberet nouum esse","la","textual","Sense obscure. Perhaps read *Si suppleret* and take *per primam … per secundam* to refer to the two ways (the term vs the formal *ratio* of filiation). B: *haberet nouum quod est impossibile per secundam*, omitting *esse* and *vero non*. B checked.","uncertain")
n("n1183","s065-08","sequaces Scoti","la","source","The thesis that relation is caused by what produces the opposite foundation has not been located in Scotus or a named Scotist.","to-verify")
n("n1184","s065-09","5. phisicorum","la","source","Aristotle, *Phys.* V 2, 225b11–13 denies that there is motion in the category of relation; the commentators (Averroes) teach that relation follows motion *per accidens*. B: *ii. phi.*, wrong. B checked.","certain")
n("n1185","s065-09","abstractionem graduum","la","textual","*abstractionem* is probably for *subtractionem* (the counterpart of *susceptionem*); the translation renders the sense.","conjecture")
n("n1186","s065-07","by the first [way]","en","translation","The sentence is obscure in A and B; see the Latin note. The translation is tentative.")
n("n1187","s065-05","the existence of the same [foundation remaining]","en","translation","*cum existentia eiusdem*: the foundation still exists.")
